## What happened

Apple removed DSA support from its **Security.framework** / **CommonCrypto** libraries. .NET's managed crypto on macOS delegates to the OS-provided primitives, so once Apple dropped DSA, `DSA.Create()` throws **`PlatformNotSupportedException`** on macOS in .NET 11. It worked in .NET 10 only because the older macOS SDK still exposed the (already-deprecated) DSA APIs.

## How to fix it

**Option A – Migrate off DSA (recommended).** DSA is a legacy algorithm (FIPS 186-4 withdrew DSA for signing in 2023). Switch to **ECDSA** or **Ed25519** for new signatures and re-sign any artifacts you control.

**Option B – Verify legacy signatures via OpenSSL.** If you must keep verifying existing DSA signatures, use the **BouncyCastle** managed crypto library, which carries its own DSA implementation with no OS dependency:

```bash
dotnet add package BouncyCastle.Cryptography
```

```csharp
using Org.BouncyCastle.Crypto.Parameters;
using Org.BouncyCastle.Crypto.Signers;
using Org.BouncyCastle.Security;

bool VerifyDsaSignature(byte[] publicKeyBytes, byte[] message, byte[] signature)
{
    var publicKey = (DsaPublicKeyParameters)PublicKeyFactory.CreateKey(publicKeyBytes);
    var signer = new DsaSigner();
    signer.Init(false, publicKey);

    // Hash the message yourself (SHA-256, SHA-1, etc. — match the original scheme)
    var digest = DigestUtilities.GetDigest("SHA-256");
    digest.BlockUpdate(message, 0, message.Length);
    var hash = new byte[digest.GetDigestSize()];
    digest.DoFinal(hash, 0);

    // Decode the DER signature into (r, s)
    var seq = (Org.BouncyCastle.Asn1.Asn1Sequence)
        Org.BouncyCastle.Asn1.Asn1Object.FromByteArray(signature);
    var r = ((Org.BouncyCastle.Asn1.DerInteger)seq[0]).Value;
    var s = ((Org.BouncyCastle.Asn1.DerInteger)seq[1]).Value;

    return signer.VerifySignature(hash, r, s);
}
```

This works identically on Linux, Windows, and macOS with no OS crypto dependency.

**Option C – Guard with a runtime check** if you only need DSA on some platforms:

```csharp
if (!OperatingSystem.IsMacOS())
{
    using var dsa = DSA.Create();
    // ...
}
```

### TL;DR

| Approach | Effort | Cross-platform |
|---|---|---|
| Migrate to ECDSA/Ed25519 | Medium | ✅ |
| BouncyCastle for legacy verify | Low | ✅ |
| Skip DSA on macOS | Low | ❌ (partial) |

For a library that must run everywhere and only *verifies* legacy signatures, **BouncyCastle** is the lowest-friction fix.
